WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.536
Webhook security in Python protects event-driven integrations that can
automatically change application state.

2
00:00:06.536 --> 00:00:13.805
A webhook endpoint is not trustworthy just because a request reaches it,
and a valid signature is not the end of the security story.

3
00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:25.209
The handler must establish source, integrity, freshness, expected event
type, payload structure, authorization context, tenant mapping, and
business meaning before it performs sensitive actions.

4
00:00:25.209 --> 00:00:37.214
Strong designs validate source and integrity, protect shared secrets,
resist replay, handle duplicate delivery safely, validate payloads,
enforce authorization, process events reliably, and log carefully.

5
00:00:37.214 --> 00:00:40.215
Freshness controls reduce acceptance of old events.

6
00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:42.883
Idempotency prevents duplicate side effects.

7
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:48.351
Queues can improve reliability when they preserve validation and
authorization expectations.

8
00:00:48.351 --> 00:00:54.420
Schema checks and local lookups keep verified payloads from becoming
blindly trusted business decisions.

9
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.688
Operations complete the control model.

10
00:00:56.688 --> 00:01:06.158
Tests should cover invalid signatures, stale events, duplicates,
unsupported event types, payload failures, tenant-boundary issues,
retries, and logging safety.

11
00:01:06.158 --> 00:01:14.294
Monitoring should show validation failures, duplicate rates, event volume,
queue delays, retry storms, and downstream dependency problems.

12
00:01:14.294 --> 00:01:22.631
Incident response should support secret rotation, provider coordination,
event reconciliation, exposure assessment, and regression testing.

13
00:01:22.631 --> 00:01:31.567
The goal is predictable, authorized, observable webhook processing that
supports automation without exposing data, credentials, or unsafe state
changes.

14
00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:43.238
Secure webhook handlers make trust decisions explicit, keep secrets narrow
and protected, tolerate repeated events, fail safely, and preserve enough
telemetry for operators to understand what happened.

15
00:01:43.238 --> 00:01:47.640
That is what turns a simple callback URL into a reliable integration
boundary.
